<article>
	<div class="intro">
		<h1>Decision workshops</h1>
		<p class="lede"><span class="gradient-text">You leave with a decision the same day</span>. Next time, someone on your team can run the same meeting without me.</p>

		<p>I run a half-day, in-person session so a team can make one real decision, what to ship, what to cut, which direction to take with the people who have to live with it in the room. 
		
		<p>You leave with a choice, owners, and next steps, not a wall of notes. I also leave a small kit, a host script and the materials and templates that stays with the team.</p>
	</div>

	<div class="what-happens">
	<h2>What happens</h2>
	<ol class="steps">
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Preparation (1 hour)</p>
			<h3>Intake: one decision, who must live with it, what <em>done</em> looks like</h3>
			<p>A written decision question, not a vague alignment session</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Half-day, in person</p>
			<h3>Generate options, vote with criteria, discuss, name next steps. Photograph the wall.</h3>
			<p>A choice, owners, and a date</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Leave-behind</p>
			<h3>Host script, plus the materials and templates we used. One named next host.</h3>
			<p>Your team can run it again. I am optional.</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
	</div>

	<aside class="fit">
		<h2 class="sr-only">Are we a fit?</h2>
		<section>
			<h2>Good fit</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>One stuck decision (what to ship, what to cut, which direction)</li>
				<li>A design lead, founder, or ED who will be in the room</li>
				<li>A team of about 6–16, in the NY Metro area or in a space you already have</li>
				<li>Someone who will name a next host before we leave</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>Not this</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Open-ended team-building with no decision</li>
				<li>A deck, or Zoom across twelve time zones</li>
				<li>A retainer to run every meeting</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</aside>

	<section class="faq">
		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Who has to be in the room, and for how long?</summary>
			<p>The people who have to live with the decision, plus a design lead, founder, or ED who will be there. About 6–16 people. Half a day, in person, in the NY Metro area or in a space you already have. About an hour of intake before that, so we walk in with a written decision question.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>What if we still don’t decide?</summary>
			<p>The point of the session is one real choice, not a wall of notes. If the room is split, we still leave with the options, who owns the next step, and a date. I will not dress up a non-decision as alignment.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Do you do this on Zoom?</summary>
			<p>No. In person, one stuck decision. Half a day in the NY Metro area or in a space you already have.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Will you just keep running our meetings?</summary>
			<p>No. I leave a small kit and we name a next host before I go, so your team can run it again. I am optional after that. This is not a retainer.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
			<p>Usually $500–$1,500 for the preparation, half-day workshop, and the leave-behind. It can vary depending on the decision, the size of the room, and the type of client.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>How do we start?</summary>
			<p>Message me on LinkedIn with the decision you are stuck on. We’ll see if it’s a fit.</p>
		</details>
	</section>

